WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.316
The team at PUggs is excited
to simplify the development

00:00:03.316 --> 00:00:07.285
of their conversational experience
using Dialogflow CX.

00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:10.133
Stick around to see it all in action.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:13.125
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:18.774
Hi, I'm Priyanka Vergadia,

00:00:18.774 --> 00:00:21.243
and in this episode
of <i>Deconstructing Chatbots</i>,

00:00:21.243 --> 00:00:23.273
we will help our friends at PUggs

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:25.280
create a conversational experience

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.440
for their customer support
using Dialogflow CX.

00:00:28.836 --> 00:00:30.745
Before we dive into the console, though,

00:00:30.745 --> 00:00:33.279
let's lay out our use case
requirements first.

00:00:34.003 --> 00:00:38.092
We know that most of their user requests
are to order dog shoes,

00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:41.111
so it makes sense to start
with the order flow first.

00:00:41.111 --> 00:00:44.728
In this flow, we want to collect
order information from the user,

00:00:44.728 --> 00:00:47.343
including the size
and the color of the shoes,

00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:49.397
and then present a confirmation.

00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:52.196
If the user confirms, we end the flow,

00:00:52.196 --> 00:00:54.199
and if they want to edit the order,

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:57.029
then we gather the new size
and color from them,

00:00:57.029 --> 00:00:58.899
and then place the order.

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:01.586
Now that we know what we are building,

00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:04.003
let's head to Dialogflow CX console.

00:01:04.003 --> 00:01:07.188
The easiest way is to get there
from the documentation.

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:10.157
Create a new project,
make sure you enable <i>Billing</i>,

00:01:10.157 --> 00:01:12.207
and the Dialogflow API.

00:01:12.207 --> 00:01:14.876
Then we go back
into the Dialogflow CX console

00:01:14.876 --> 00:01:17.577
and click on the project we just created.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.726
It prompts us to create an agent.

00:01:19.726 --> 00:01:21.910
That's exactly what we want to do.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:25.861
We name it, select the location
where we want to deploy it,

00:01:25.861 --> 00:01:28.596
and the timezone, and the language,

00:01:28.596 --> 00:01:30.562
and we're good to create.

00:01:30.562 --> 00:01:33.195
Now, notice that within a project,

00:01:33.195 --> 00:01:35.463
we can create multiple agents.

00:01:35.902 --> 00:01:39.520
We have our <i>Default Start Flow</i>
with our <i>Start</i> page,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.392
which comes with
the <i>Default Welcome Intent.</i>

00:01:42.392 --> 00:01:44.846
So let's go ahead and test it.

00:01:44.846 --> 00:01:48.446
At this point, all it does
is greet the user.

00:01:48.446 --> 00:01:51.982
We want to create a <i>Transition Route</i>
from the <i>Start</i> page

00:01:51.982 --> 00:01:53.901
that leads to the <i>Order</i> flow.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.368
Create new <i>Intent</i>.

00:01:55.368 --> 00:01:57.784
Let's name it and add
some training phrases.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.818
Let's add some basic ones such as,

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:01.817
"I would like to place an order."

00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:05.837
But we also need to add
some specific phrases with <i>color</i>.

00:02:05.837 --> 00:02:10.050
Let's add "I want to buy
green shoes for my pup."

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.884
As soon as we add that,
notice that the color parameter

00:02:13.884 --> 00:02:18.067
automatically gets created
with <i>@sys.color</i> Entity type.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.688
And this color parameter
will be stored in the session for us

00:02:21.688 --> 00:02:23.899
to access in other pages.

00:02:23.899 --> 00:02:28.069
Also, since the user
has already provided the color,

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:31.254
our agent will not ask
for that information,

00:02:31.254 --> 00:02:33.872
providing a more natural experience.

00:02:34.568 --> 00:02:37.627
Now, let's add
another example with the size.

00:02:37.627 --> 00:02:40.660
"Wanna get large shoes for my husky."

00:02:40.937 --> 00:02:42.805
Now, we see that the <i>large</i>

00:02:42.805 --> 00:02:46.173
is not automatically identified
as a parameter

00:02:46.173 --> 00:02:49.637
because size is unique to PUggs use case.

00:02:50.142 --> 00:02:51.630
So let's fix that.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.830
But before we do that,
add a <i>Transition</i> to <i>new Page</i>

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.435
where we will collect
information and save it.

00:02:57.972 --> 00:03:02.005
Let's go into <i>Manage &gt; Entity Types</i>,
and then <i>Create New</i>.

00:03:02.005 --> 00:03:06.488
Name it "size," and add <i>small,
medium</i>, <i>large</i> size in there

00:03:06.488 --> 00:03:08.041
with some synonyms.

00:03:08.774 --> 00:03:11.224
Now, while we are on the <i>Manage</i> tab,

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.675
let's go into the <i>Intents</i>

00:03:12.675 --> 00:03:15.826
to see if we can add
our "size" parameter now.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:20.062
Add one or two more examples
with both <i>size</i> and <i>color</i>

00:03:20.062 --> 00:03:21.424
to add some variety.

00:03:21.424 --> 00:03:23.847
Let's head over to our
<i>Collect Information</i> page

00:03:23.847 --> 00:03:25.565
and add the <i>Entry dialogue</i>

00:03:25.565 --> 00:03:26.695
to let the user know

00:03:26.695 --> 00:03:29.149
that we will create
some more information now.

00:03:29.149 --> 00:03:30.979
Then add the <i>Parameter</i>.

00:03:30.979 --> 00:03:32.801
<i>Size</i> is a required parameter,

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.918
and if the user does not provide it,

00:03:34.918 --> 00:03:38.072
we want to prompt them
with the <i>Fulfillment</i> here.

00:03:38.072 --> 00:03:40.655
We repeat the same for <i>color</i> as well.

00:03:40.655 --> 00:03:42.803
With that, we are ready to define

00:03:42.803 --> 00:03:45.441
our <i>Transition routes</i> from this page.

00:03:45.441 --> 00:03:48.425
And in this case, we don't need
to trigger an <i>Intent</i>.

00:03:48.425 --> 00:03:52.394
All we need is to make sure
our <i>Parameters</i> are filled in.

00:03:52.394 --> 00:03:57.894
So we look for the condition to match:
<i>$page.params.status = FINAL</i>

00:03:57.894 --> 00:04:01.764
Once all the <i>Parameters</i>
are defined and collected,

00:04:01.764 --> 00:04:05.400
which means both <i>size</i>
and <i>color</i>, in this case,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.500
that's when the <i>status</i> will turn to <i>FINAL</i>.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.419
This is also where we can match
other conditions,

00:04:11.419 --> 00:04:15.405
such as if the <i>$page.params.color = RED</i>,

00:04:15.405 --> 00:04:17.555
then send to a "sorry" page

00:04:17.555 --> 00:04:20.672
because that color is not available
in the inventory.

00:04:21.031 --> 00:04:25.150
Once the <i>status</i> equals <i>FINAL</i>,
condition is met.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.904
We would route the user
to the new <i>confirmation</i> page.

00:04:29.407 --> 00:04:30.736
In the <i>confirmation</i> page,

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.821
let's first add the <i>Entry dialogue</i>

00:04:32.821 --> 00:04:35.639
to share what they have selected to buy.

00:04:35.639 --> 00:04:39.773
We can access the <i>Parameters</i>
in the session by using the <i>$</i> sign.

00:04:40.274 --> 00:04:43.992
We don't have any <i>Parameter</i>
to add for this page.

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:45.627
For the <i>Transition routes</i>,

00:04:45.627 --> 00:04:48.091
we want to have a "yes" and a "no" route.

00:04:48.091 --> 00:04:51.397
For "yes" path, let's create a new <i>Intent</i>

00:04:51.397 --> 00:04:53.732
and call it "confirmation.yes,"

00:04:53.732 --> 00:04:57.464
and provide a few <i>Training phrases</i>
that indicate "yes."

00:04:58.038 --> 00:05:02.303
<i>Save</i> the <i>Intent</i> and then add
the <i>Transition</i> page as "Success."

00:05:02.303 --> 00:05:04.558
Do the same thing for "no" route.

00:05:04.558 --> 00:05:06.556
<i>Success</i> page is easy at this point.

00:05:06.556 --> 00:05:09.844
All we need to do is add
a nice <i>Entry dialogue</i>.

00:05:09.844 --> 00:05:12.790
For the <i>Transition route</i>,
add "true" in the <i>Condition</i>

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.329
to force and select <i>End Flow</i>
as the <i>Transition page</i>.

00:05:16.329 --> 00:05:18.176
Now, the <i>Failure</i> page.

00:05:18.176 --> 00:05:21.131
We want to see if the user wants
to change their selection,

00:05:21.131 --> 00:05:23.333
or they just don't want to buy today.

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.733
For that, we add the <i>Entry dialogue</i>.

00:05:25.733 --> 00:05:27.935
And then add a <i>Transition Route</i>.

00:05:27.935 --> 00:05:29.147
If they say "no,"

00:05:29.147 --> 00:05:32.232
we just want to add
a <i>GoodBye</i> page, quite simple.

00:05:32.232 --> 00:05:33.655
But if they say "yes,"

00:05:33.655 --> 00:05:36.344
then we send them back
to the start of the <i>Flow</i>

00:05:36.344 --> 00:05:39.011
to make their <i>color</i>
and <i>size</i> selections.

00:05:39.345 --> 00:05:40.963
Now, let's test it.

00:05:41.813 --> 00:05:44.180
That doesn't quite work.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:47.830
And that's because the <i>Parameters</i>
are already filled.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.900
We need to clear out the <i>Parameters</i>

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.817
before the state changes
to the <i>Start</i> page.

00:05:53.355 --> 00:05:55.636
And we do that in the <i>Parameter presets</i>

00:05:55.636 --> 00:05:59.523
in the <i>yes</i> Intent Transition
of the <i>Failure</i> page.

00:05:59.944 --> 00:06:03.824
Let's test it again, and we see
that the <i>Flow</i> is all set.

00:06:03.843 --> 00:06:06.293
Alright, so that was a lot.

00:06:06.293 --> 00:06:09.612
We created the entire
<i>Order Flow</i> from scratch

00:06:09.612 --> 00:06:11.612
by creating a bunch of pages.

00:06:11.612 --> 00:06:15.159
We also learned how <i>Intents</i>,
<i>Parameters</i>, and <i>Entities</i> work

00:06:15.159 --> 00:06:17.148
in conjunction with the <i>Pages</i>.

00:06:17.495 --> 00:06:19.983
I am very excited for the next episode

00:06:19.983 --> 00:06:23.480
where we will extend the PUggs
conversation experience further

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.573
by adding multiple <i>Flows</i>.

00:06:25.573 --> 00:06:28.188
Until then, I look forward
to seeing your thoughts

00:06:28.188 --> 00:06:30.854
on this episode in the comments below.

00:06:30.854 --> 00:06:33.315
♪ [music] ♪

